      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "The farmer appears to be uprooting a noxious thistle that has emerged among his cultivated tomato plants.",
          "grammar": "appear to be＋現在分詞 / 関係代名詞that / 現在完了形",
          "ja": "農家は栽培中のトマトの間に生えてきた有害なアザミを根こそぎ引き抜いているようです。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The weed's tall stem, jagged leaves, and extensive roots distinguish it clearly from the surrounding crop.",
          "grammar": "並列主語 / distinguish A from B",
          "ja": "その雑草の高い茎、ぎざぎざした葉、広がった根は、周囲の作物とは明らかに異なっています。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "A noxious weed can be detrimental to agriculture because it competes with crops for limited water, light, and nutrients.",
          "grammar": "can / because / compete with A for B",
          "ja": "有害雑草は限られた水、光、栄養分を作物と奪い合うため、農業に悪影響を及ぼす可能性があります。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "By grasping the plant near its base, the farmer is attempting to remove the entire root system rather than merely cutting off the visible foliage.",
          "grammar": "By＋動名詞 / attempt to / rather than＋動名詞",
          "ja": "植物の根元をつかむことで、農家は目に見える葉だけを切るのではなく、根全体を除去しようとしています。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "If part of the root were left in the soil, the thistle might regenerate and continue encroaching on the cultivated area.",
          "grammar": "仮定法過去 / might / continue＋動名詞",
          "ja": "もし根の一部が土の中に残れば、アザミが再生して耕作地への侵入を続ける可能性があります。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Removing invasive vegetation before it produces seeds can reduce the likelihood of a wider infestation.",
          "grammar": "動名詞主語 / before / can",
          "ja": "侵略的な植物が種を作る前に除去することで、さらに広範囲へ蔓延する可能性を低下させることができます。",
